## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a streaming gate with per-user policy, token verification, per-user caches, and idempotence considerations under multi-tenant load.

## Key Concepts
- Streaming token validation per user
- TTL-based per-user caches
- Exact vs at-least-once semantics in gates
- Canary rollout and rollback safety

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: gate events with per-user tokens
function processEvent(e, tokenStore) {
  const t = tokenStore.get(e.userId);
  if (!t) return {forward:false, reason:'no-token'};
  if (Date.now() >= t.expiry) return {forward:false, reason:'expired'};
  if (!verifySignature(e, t.signature)) return {forward:false, reason:'bad-signature'};
  return {forward:true};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would token revocation during peak load affect latency and correctness?
- How would you test clock skew and cross-partition consistency for token expiry?

